story. A lot of them, it's immortalized in the film Missing with Jack Lemmon and Sissy Spacek. There was a guy called Charlie Horman. He was a Harvard graduate who had gone to Santiago to try and become a writer and a filmmaker. He'd been really into the Chilean regime. By hideous mischance, he was in the seaside town of Viña del Mar when the coup broke out. And he's got into conversation in a bar or something like that, or in a hotel with some Americans. And the Americans said, oh, we work for the US Navy. We're just down here doing a job. And it's done. We're going to go home now. And he's like, oh, what's the job? And the mood turns very icy. He goes back to Santiago. He is eventually rounded
故事。他们中的很多人，这个故事在杰克·莱蒙和茜茜·斯派塞克主演的电影《失踪》（Missing）中得到了永生。有一个人叫查理·霍曼（Charlie Horman）。他是哈佛大学毕业生，曾前往圣地亚哥试图成为一名作家和电影制作人。他一直对智利政权非常感兴趣。由于一次可怕的阴差阳错，政变爆发时，他正身处海滨小镇比尼亚德尔马。他在一家酒吧或类似的地方，或者在一家酒店里与一些美国人交谈。美国人说，哦，我们为美国海军工作。我们只是到这里来执行一个任务。任务完成了。我们现在要回家了。他说，哦，什么任务？气氛顿时变得非常冰冷。他回到了圣地亚哥。他最终被围捕。

